{
  "job": "refine",
  "want": "character",
  "rank": 8,
  "short": "character only",
  "title": {
    "zh": "换模型精修·只改人物",
    "en": "Refine only the character"
  },
  "about": {
    "zh": "自动抠出人物，换另一个模型只重画人物，边缘慢慢减弱，场景原样不动，另存一张。",
    "en": "Cuts the character out; another model redraws only it, fading out at its edge, the scene left as it was; saved beside it."
  },
  "source": {
    "zh": "常见的抠图加渐变遮罩局部重画（ComfyUI 自带的 Differential Diffusion），强度按 2026-11-10 的人物重画对照定",
    "en": "The common cut-out with a graded-mask repaint (ComfyUI's own Differential Diffusion), its strength from a character redraw comparison of 2026-11-10"
  },
  "packs": {
    "InspyrenetRembg": "comfyui-inspyrenet-rembg"
  },
  "nodes": {
    "second_model": {
      "class_type": "CheckpointLoaderSimple",
      "like": "$loader",
      "inputs": {}
    },
    "second_positive": {
      "class_type": "CLIPTextEncode",
      "like": "$sampler.positive",
      "inputs": {
        "clip": ["second_model", 1]
      }
    },
    "second_negative": {
      "class_type": "CLIPTextEncode",
      "like": "$sampler.negative",
      "inputs": {
        "clip": ["second_model", 1]
      }
    },
    "cut": {
      "class_type": "InspyrenetRembg",
      "inputs": {
        "image": ["$save.images", "*"],
        "torchscript_jit": "default"
      }
    },
    "solid": {
      "class_type": "ThresholdMask",
      "inputs": {
        "mask": ["cut", 1],
        "value": 0.5
      }
    },
    "edge": {
      "class_type": "GrowMask",
      "inputs": {
        "mask": ["solid", 0],
        "expand": 12,
        "tapered_corners": true
      }
    },
    "as_picture": {
      "class_type": "MaskToImage",
      "inputs": {
        "mask": ["edge", 0]
      }
    },
    "fade": {
      "class_type": "ImageBlur",
      "inputs": {
        "image": ["as_picture", 0],
        "blur_radius": 31,
        "sigma": 0.5
      }
    },
    "area_mask": {
      "class_type": "ImageToMask",
      "inputs": {
        "image": ["fade", 0],
        "channel": "red"
      }
    },
    "soft": {
      "class_type": "DifferentialDiffusion",
      "inputs": {
        "model": ["second_model", 0]
      }
    },
    "encode": {
      "class_type": "VAEEncode",
      "inputs": {
        "pixels": ["$save.images", "*"],
        "vae": ["second_model", 2]
      }
    },
    "area": {
      "class_type": "SetLatentNoiseMask",
      "inputs": {
        "samples": ["encode", 0],
        "mask": ["area_mask", 0]
      }
    },
    "redraw": {
      "class_type": "KSampler",
      "like": "$sampler",
      "inputs": {
        "model": ["soft", 0],
        "positive": ["second_positive", 0],
        "negative": ["second_negative", 0],
        "latent_image": ["area", 0],
        "denoise": 0.45
      }
    },
    "decode": {
      "class_type": "VAEDecode",
      "inputs": {
        "samples": ["redraw", 0],
        "vae": ["second_model", 2]
      }
    },
    "paste": {
      "class_type": "ImageCompositeMasked",
      "inputs": {
        "destination": ["$save.images", "*"],
        "source": ["decode", 0],
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "resize_source": false,
        "mask": ["area_mask", 0]
      }
    },
    "save": {
      "class_type": "SaveImage",
      "inputs": {
        "images": ["paste", 0],
        "filename_prefix": "refined_character"
      }
    },
    "look": {
      "class_type": "PreviewImage",
      "inputs": {
        "images": ["fade", 0]
      }
    }
  },
  "after": "The redraw's loader (second_model) starts as the same checkpoint: set_model it to the model the user wants for the character (ask_user, search_models), add_lora a character or style LoRA onto it if they want one, and write its prompts (second_positive, second_negative, copied from the first) in that model's style. Then run_workflow; the picture is saved beside it (prefix refined_character), the scene the same to the pixel. Denoise 0.45: face, hair and clothes take the second model's look and the pose stays; 0.3 changes little; at 0.6 the face changes more and colours fade. The preview shows what is redrawn (white, fading at the edge): part of the character missing, or the background in it, say so.",
  "gives": {
    "sampler": "redraw",
    "save": "save"
  },
  "own_model": {
    "nodes": ["second_model"],
    "copies_loras": false
  },
  "notes": "The character's mask grows 12 px and is blurred about 15 px, so the redraw fades out at its edge; Differential Diffusion makes the mask's grey a weaker redraw, and the paste-back keeps everything outside it as it was. In the 2026-11-10 comparison (an Anima picture, RealSkin redrawing the character) this way at 0.45 changed the character about 5.5% on average and the scene 0.03%; the coat stayed on the bench. A small character in a wide picture gets few pixels for its face: repaint it (inpaint_crop_stitch) instead. The cut-out takes what stands out in front, often with what the character sits on or holds (a bench, an umbrella, a bag): redrawn with it, so where they touch still fits.",
  "models": [],
  "tested": {
    "gpu": "RTX 4050 Laptop",
    "vram_gb": 6,
    "date": "2026-11-10",
    "runs": [
      {
        "model": "Anima (Harem 2.9B, then RealSkin 1.3 on the character, denoise 0.45)",
        "size": "1440×1024",
        "seconds": 242
      }
    ]
  },
  "variants": {
    "anima": {
      "nodes": {
        "second_model": {
          "class_type": "UNETLoader",
          "like": "$loader",
          "inputs": {}
        },
        "cut": {
          "class_type": "InspyrenetRembg",
          "inputs": {
            "image": ["$save.images", "*"],
            "torchscript_jit": "default"
          }
        },
        "solid": {
          "class_type": "ThresholdMask",
          "inputs": {
            "mask": ["cut", 1],
            "value": 0.5
          }
        },
        "edge": {
          "class_type": "GrowMask",
          "inputs": {
            "mask": ["solid", 0],
            "expand": 12,
            "tapered_corners": true
          }
        },
        "as_picture": {
          "class_type": "MaskToImage",
          "inputs": {
            "mask": ["edge", 0]
          }
        },
        "fade": {
          "class_type": "ImageBlur",
          "inputs": {
            "image": ["as_picture", 0],
            "blur_radius": 31,
            "sigma": 0.5
          }
        },
        "area_mask": {
          "class_type": "ImageToMask",
          "inputs": {
            "image": ["fade", 0],
            "channel": "red"
          }
        },
        "soft": {
          "class_type": "DifferentialDiffusion",
          "inputs": {
            "model": ["second_model", 0]
          }
        },
        "encode": {
          "class_type": "VAEEncode",
          "inputs": {
            "pixels": ["$save.images", "*"],
            "vae": ["$decode.vae", "*"]
          }
        },
        "area": {
          "class_type": "SetLatentNoiseMask",
          "inputs": {
            "samples": ["encode", 0],
            "mask": ["area_mask", 0]
          }
        },
        "redraw": {
          "class_type": "KSampler",
          "like": "$sampler",
          "inputs": {
            "model": ["soft", 0],
            "positive": ["$sampler.positive", "*"],
            "negative": ["$sampler.negative", "*"],
            "latent_image": ["area", 0],
            "denoise": 0.45
          }
        },
        "decode": {
          "class_type": "VAEDecode",
          "inputs": {
            "samples": ["redraw", 0],
            "vae": ["$decode.vae", "*"]
          }
        },
        "paste": {
          "class_type": "ImageCompositeMasked",
          "inputs": {
            "destination": ["$save.images", "*"],
            "source": ["decode", 0],
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "resize_source": false,
            "mask": ["area_mask", 0]
          }
        },
        "save": {
          "class_type": "SaveImage",
          "inputs": {
            "images": ["paste", 0],
            "filename_prefix": "refined_character"
          }
        },
        "look": {
          "class_type": "PreviewImage",
          "inputs": {
            "images": ["fade", 0]
          }
        }
      },
      "after": "On this Anima model the redraw's loader (second_model) is a UNET loader that starts as the canvas's model; it reuses the canvas's text encoder, VAE and prompts. set_model it to the other Anima model the user wants for the character (ask_user, search_models); a LoRA on the first model is not on it: add_lora it onto second_model when the user wants that look kept. Then run_workflow; the picture is saved beside it (prefix refined_character), the scene the same to the pixel. Denoise 0.45: face, hair and clothes take the second model's look and the pose stays; 0.3 changes little; at 0.6 the face changes more and colours fade. The preview shows what is redrawn (white, fading at the edge): part of the character missing, or the background in it, say so."
    }
  }
}
